tickets.body:
Static only: ildasm or REA over the pinned v1.4.8 DLLs, no game launch.

For each path record the installed call site, which culture or template it reads, and the narrowest point where a per-people template can be substituted (model override, campaign behaviour or Harmony patch):

1. volunteers (`Culture.BasicTroop`, `EliteBasicTroop`);
2. upgrade targets;
3. militia;
4. garrisons;
5. caravans (guards and caravan master);
6. villagers (villager parties and village LocationCharacters);
7. bandits;
8. town LocationCharacters (townsfolk, merchants, guards).

Note how each path meets the overhaul's population system (MMR-174, MMR-179) and the peoples epic's people cultures (MMR-207, MMR-209). Start from what the character-overhaul red team already traced (docs/research/character-overhaul-dd2-redteam.md, D10 and §4.1) instead of re-deriving it.

Checks: the document covers all eight paths; no game launch.

Inventory what each presentation culture supplies today (troop tree, civilian characters, clothing, settlement scenes, buildings) and which peoples borrow it (`worldgen/policies/culture-presentations.json`, the people registry of peoples MMR-204).

Propose, per people, either its own content or a sharing rule (for example hill and frosthold dwarf on dwarf content), with:
- rough asset counts;
- the art route (overhaul D2: dd2-derived development assets with lineage, then the clean-replacement epic ep_01m57w9twf9yywa7wshwcyw42r);
- whether the overhaul's race-body equipment fits (MMR-227) cover its clothing.

The user picks the table at the sprint checkpoint. Desk work; no game launch.
